From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:21:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: admit Works from a compact ledger, not flight
 scans

reserve_flight walked every unretired flight up to seven times per render
(queue cap, per stage the channel targets, lane Work count and lane heads)
and read three channel registers per stage over MMIO, rebuilding the whole
firmware MainConfig to find them. On Dota (#174) it was 2.5 us per Work.

Keep a ledger next to the flights, updated at their two push sites and at
retirement: per-lane Work, load and owned-entry totals, plus compact
(lane, head) and (channel, target) lists for the half-ring checks, which
keep their exact semantics. Cache each work channel's read, done and tail
cursors. The driver is the tail's only writer, and stale read and done
cursors only under-report room, so the registers are reread only when the
cached view has no room; a reread tail that disagrees with the cache is
reported. Channel routes come from a per-channel helper.

The watchdog read the clock once per flight on every pump pass and wrote
every flight on each retirement. It now keeps one progress timestamp and
reads the clock once per pass, with the same per-flight ages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
